{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1391160-actual-play-magnum-opus","id":1391160,"title":"[Actual Play] Magnum Opus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-24T04:34:00-07:00","id":1391160,"title":"[Actual Play] Magnum Opus","content":"<span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>First, there is only pain. It defines your existence and the borders of your body. It seems almost\u2026 familiar. You realise you are able to categorise it. The burning in your head? A fractured skull. The hot, itchy feeling across your arms are cuts, the sharp aches in your chest broken ribs. There\u2019s another pain, though, a pain that eclipses all the others and makes them seem insignificant. It\u2019s feels like a hole in your chest, a burning cold, a sorrow without limit. </i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>You try to move a hand experimentally only to find you cannot. You try to draw a breath and take in lungfuls of dust. Choking, you realise you\u2019ve been buried alive.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Strength. You need </i>strength<i>. The thought sends fire into your muscles and you strain, rocks cascading off you as rise from the rubble, pulling yourself free with a sound somewhere between a cough and a roar.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>It is dark. You wish for a lantern, a candle, a torch and to your amazement the thought brings warmth to your flesh. Suddenly you are aglow, the dark shadows of your bones visible beneath your radiant flesh. The light is sufficient to see. You\u2019re in a cave\u2026 no, a ruin. You can see now that a portion of the ceiling collapsed and buried you. </i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Your memories are awhirl. Words and concepts float in and out of your mind, words like \u2018pilgrimage\u2019, \u2018daughter\u2019\u2026 You look for something to anchor yourself, and you\u2019re surprised to find it. There is writing on the walls, etched into dressed stone. Flakes of paint and lacquer suggest this room was once more grandiose but time has worn away all beauty and gilt and left only the words beneath. The words are written in Latin, in Greek, in Arabic and English, French and Manding\u2026 In places, one script is used with the grammar and words of another language. It\u2019s a resource that would eclipse the Rosetta stone, an almost impossible linguistic challenge, but you can read it. The words in this ancient chamber are written in handwriting you recognise. Your own.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>You try to find the start of it all, all too aware that in places the walls are too damaged to read and the rubble from which you emerged is blocking off sections of text. </i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Dim memories of Greece stir in you, but details escape and the text is long-faded. There was a creator\u2026 a father? A lover? You remember\u2026 pain\u2026 Sadness. </i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Your eyes and fingers follow the text as it transitions from Greek into Latin and memories flood back. Rome, the self-proclaimed greatest city. A city of vice and decadence, a place where you came to understand the beauty and horror of humankind\u2019s impurity. </i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">***</span></span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Out of character introduction: As we\u2019ve all got a lot more free time for RPGs for some reason recently, a long-time player-collaborator and I started something new. This player lives in a different city and was pretty busy in the Before Times, making online play essentially impossible, so we normally play 2-3 marathon games (generally played over a long weekend with approximately 24-36 hours of actual gameplay) a year. This, and difficulties scheduling with my regular local group, led to this game.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This game is me combining my two impossible grail games into a horribly ambitious ur-game. I\u2019m a big Chronicles of Darkness fan (and occasional contributor) and, like many people, consider Promethean: The Created my favourite game I never play. The amount of buy-in needed from players, the difficulty capturing the mood without being too twee or po-faced\u2026 It\u2019s a tricky line to walk. I doubt anyone clicked this without knowledgeof Promethean, but just in case, it's a game of created things (Frankenstein's Monsters, golems) learning to be human with the hope they can actually <i>become </i>human. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The other grail idea, something I had back when I first read Mummy: The Curse, was to play a chronicle set over multiple time periods (each with a theme) with an amnesiac protagonist in the modern era piecing their life together through flashbacks. Now would be a good time to say <i>Planescape Torment</i> is one of my favourite computer games, wouldn\u2019t it? There <i>will</i> be similarities and outright references from day one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So this game (which does ignore/change one or two things about Promethean lifespan from 2e) is set across centuries, following a Promethean through different eras, in which they walk different Refinements (philosophies/paths/ways of living, for those unfamiliar with the setting) to understand themselves and eventually become human, piecing together their memories before a climax in the modern day.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Our protagonist is a Galateid who awoke in Greece around 100BC. Named for the muse Melpomene, she\u2019ll wear other names. In Rome, she is Pomponia. In Tudor England she is Melody Pomeney. In the modern era she\u2019s Melanie.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The first session, and first era we\u2019re playing in (though not the first one in the main character\u2019s life) is Rome in 62AD and she's walking the Refinement of Cobalt.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">***</span></span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pomponia is relatively new to Rome, having previously served as a medici with the legions. She has come to Rome to look for humankind\u2019s impurity, having previously walked the refinement of Gold, living among people but ultimately being disappointed by them. Pomponia finds sorrow the most compelling, human emotion and has taken the role of confessor.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">To this, end her first actions to try to carve a niche among the lower echelons of Ronan society. She made inroads with a local brothel, offering her services as a private doctor, and struck up a conversation with a beggar with a missing foot. Said beggar claimed to be a former legionary, though he was evasive and unconvincing under questioning and ultimately proved to be an escape slave.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pomponia visited a haruspex and asked for her soothsaying wisdom. Dutifully, Corvina consulted the entrails and gave her a prophecy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>\u201cYour life will be long and unhappy, but I think you know this. Four men will you meet; three will be your companions on a long journey. One will ask everything and nothing of you, one will offer friendship and one will offer a partnership. One will be a friend, one a bitter enemy and one a fellow traveller.\u201d</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>\u201cWhat about the fourth?\u201d</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>\u201cThe fourth will be a lesson.\u201d</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Out of character, I want to note that this wasn\u2019t scripted or set up pre-game but was largely improvised based around ideas I had. I\u2019d told the player augurs and haruspices existed and they sought one out. Prophecies, of course, do very much belong in Promethean. Though I have rough ideas for who will be who, these aren't set in stone and the prophecy is vague is enough to give me plenty of wiggle room. One of the most exciting parts of a game set over centuries is the rare few recurring NPCs (Prometheans and other), who will grow and change (and forget) from epoch to epoch.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">That evening, the brothel\u2019s proprietor, Cilo, contacted Pomponia and had her treat an injured drunk as an audition. As she left, Pomponia noticed she was being followed. She attempted to ambush her pursuer only to find herself face-to-face with a hideous creature. A pallid face with bloodshot eyes, no nose to speak of and a nest of rotten fangs in its mouth.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhat is your name?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cPomponia.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI am called Worm.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cGood evening, worm. What can I do for you?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorm is not sure... You intrigue me. My kindred, they fear you. You smell wrong; you set our teeth on edge. They think you are a monster, an unnatural thing. Are you?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201c\u201cHow would someone who isn\u2019t breathing define unnatural?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorms looks at himself and thinks: Worm is a monster. Worm is an unnatural thing. And where others flee in horror there is Worm. Worm is curious.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThen yes. Who are your kin\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cTelling you is a crime, yet Worm fears no censure for they are afraid to speak with you. Still, I must swear you to secrecy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cNaturally.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cAll things have a shadow, yes? A dark counterpart. So too do the people of Rome. Not all that die remain dead and pass to the underworld, no, some stay on earth. The walking dead, the hungry dead. All things have a shadow; there is a shadow senate that meets in the night. You may have heard rumours that dead men race in the Circus Maximus by night, settling old scores? Not rumours. Truth.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cAnd you are one of these men?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYes.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThe shadow senate? What does it concern itself with?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThe same thing as the other senate. Prestige, who sets the laws, the interpretation of the gods\u2019 will\u2026\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He made a dismissive gesture.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cNothing interesting,\u201d Pomponia translated.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201dPrecisely. But you are interesting. It is\u2026. Difficult for me to near you,\u201d he stated, matter of factly.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cIt is no difficulty for me to be near you, though I\u2019m sorry I cause you discomfort.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cIt is good that you say. Many find it difficult to be near Worm, even his own people. That is why they call him Worm. They think it insults him. Better to be called a lion or a bear, yes? But I see how the lions and bears face in the coliseum. Better to be a worm, I am thinking? Worms thrive.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWas it your idea to seek me, then? Or a lion, or a bear?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorm\u2019s idea. The lions and bears are not concerned with you, or afraid of you. But worm does not run from things others are afraid of. It seems you are a doctor?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI am. I\u2019ve never treated the dead, though the idea is fascinating\u2026\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorm does not think the dead need doctors\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He asked where Pomponia lived; it was a difficult question to answer and Worm\u2019s inhuman visage made for quite the poker face. She gave a vague answer which he accepted; he had no difficulty finding her.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cIs there anything Worm can do for you?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cHow much do the dead have to do with the living?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWe live beside one another.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI\u2019m interested in those who suffer. Those who are struggling. If you can put me in touch with anyone that would be welcome. Anyone who might need my skills. \u201c</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorm thinks, for the first at least, you should pick up a rock, throw it and you will find someone who is suffering. There is no shortage of suffering in this great city. Worm is not often in the company of those who need a doctor, and he is often willing to provide bloodletting himself.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pomponia knew enough to understand the joke</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Worm promised to what he could, and also noted he was good at finding people. He admitted he wasn\u2019t sure what to make of Pomponia, but he viewed her as something others overlooked or feared and as such something he felt he could make use of. Pomponia asked if he could warn her if people took steps to\u2026 act on their fear. Worm promised to what he could and admitted he felt an urge to run away from her, or to fight, but promised he was good at controlling his urges.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Worm went on to ask what Pomponia was, describing himself as an owl, an eater of the dead. Pomponia described her a creation, aspiring to what he had lost. Worm scoffed a little at this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorm thinks you aspire to nothing of worth. Some might think it is terrible to be a worm, but better than being kine.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYou don\u2019t miss the life you had?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cAdapting was\u2026 difficult. But there was opportunity. Worm does not miss his old life. It is unimportant. The worm emerges from the corpse and so it was with me.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhat does worm do?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWorm enjoys being overlooked. In his own way, overlooked little worm is a powerful man. Big secret.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI have nobody to tell.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThat is why worm told you.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The two struck up their strange alliance of sorts, including a way for Pomponia to contact the apparition (scrawling his namesake in this alleyway).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Following this Pomponia went to a cauponae, a bar, and witnessed a violent altercation. Two drunken patrons were beating another man. She sat next to one of the other patrons (who weren\u2019t intervening), using Transmutations to loosen tongues to ask why the man was being attacked and why nobody was helping. She learned he was a foreigner, and thus distrusted, and the watchers were nervous about getting involved. After shaming the man she\u2019s sat by with a piercing question (\u201cWould you have interfered if it was a Roman, not a foreigner?\u201d), she followed the blood trail to assist the injured man, discovering he was a merchant from another part of Italy who had come to the city.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pomponia was surprised to be interrupted by another Promethean, a cadaverous figure. Tall, gaunt and with a face that hinted at rot.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The stranger\u2019s Measure, the sense Prometheans gain when meeting another of their kind, was similarly <i>rotten</i> feeling. There was a sense of turmoil but also a strange feeling of familiarity, of kinship.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cGood evening.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cGood evening,\u201d replied Pomponia, uncertain.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The newcomer gestured to the injured man, walking away.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhat did you learn?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cPeople think they\u2019re braver than they are. Or want to tell themselves they would be.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cA fine lesson, is it not?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cIt\u2019s similar to the one I learned moments before\u2026 but good to have confirmation.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And how does that make you feel?\u201d pressed the newcomer.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cDisappointed.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cDisappointed?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cPeople could do an awful more if they didn\u2019t tell themselves a story about why they can\u2019t.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cVery true. This disappoints you? You are not accustomed to this; it is new to you?\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYes.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cInteresting.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThis is not a new lesson for you, then.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cNo.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Silence remained for a moment before Pomponia asked the stranger his age, learning he was slightly older than her.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWe\u2019ve learned some different lessons so far, then.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cSo you have learned humankind is worthy of respect and admiration?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYes.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI fear you have learned a false lesson, but perhaps in time you will see. It seems you are looking for the right things, the impurity within\u2026 \u201c</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cPerhaps it\u2019s a difference between the individual and the whole?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cSo you\u2019re suggesting a person is good, people are bad? Am I correct in my assessment?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThat would fit my current experience, yes.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI see your model will change with evidence. Interesting. Good even. This has been enlightening.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhat have <i>you</i> learned most recently?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cRecently? Nothing .\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cMost recently, however far back that may be.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThat I am incapable of surprise.\u201c</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWe\u2019ll have to see how we can change that, then.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYes, perhaps we will,\u201d he replied with genuine warmth and a smile before walking away. Pompnia asked for his name but he had already disappeared into the night.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pomponia decided to seek out a Promethean she had seen before but never spoken with; Vigil. Vigil dresses as one of the <i>vigiles</i>, Rome\u2019s night watch/fire service. His Measure was like being plunged into icy water, though not necessarily unpleasant after the initial shock. His skin was shrivelled around his lips and eyes and he smelled of salt. His eyes glittered with curiosity. After the initial pleasantries, Vigil asked Pomponia a question</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cMay I ask you a question? I\u2019m afraid it\u2019s a philosophical question.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI can\u2019t make promises about the quality of my answer, but\u2026\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThat\u2019s alright. What can change the nature of a man?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cSorrow,\u201d Pomponia replied, after only a moment\u2019s thought. \u201cWhen you reflect on something you can grow.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cA fine answer, thank you.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhat do you believe to be the answer?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhy do you think I ask the question?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI feel I am unlikely to be the first person you\u2019ve asked.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cCorrect; I\u2019ve heard many answers. None of them felt quite right to me yet. Not to say that your answer was wrong in any way. I have heard your answer before.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cAre the people here helping you find the answer?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cPerhaps. It is a slow process, but\u2026 we must not allow ourselves to be disheartened. Just because questions do not have easy answers does not mean they should not be asked, nor that the answers will forever elude us\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cFrom what I\u2019ve seen on the street,\u201d Pomponia replied, thinking of the philosophers she\u2019d seen in the forums, \u201cthere are lots of people asking similar questions.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cYes, it is\u2026 enjoyable. I have been avoiding them of late.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhy?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cThey know me too well.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cAh.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cDo you have a question?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWhy do good people do bad things?\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cA conundrum. I have an answer, though it comes in the form of a question. Define good and define bad.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI should have anticipated that question. Working on both.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cIt is important to acknowledge when one does not know the answer. Far too many act as though they do; I have been led astray in the past.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">After this Vigil wasn\u2019t especially talkative, and was very comfortable with a contemplative silence, but he confirmed knowing about three other Prometheans (a tally that matched Pomponia\u2019s own); Calidus, a gladiator (with an increasing popularity problem) and the unnamed man Pomponia had met earlier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">They briefly discussed Calidus, noting he had made no approaches to others and they shared confusion at his choice of path.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cI don\u2019t know what lesson he\u2019s learning. I don\u2019t think I could learn the lesson in the same way.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201cWe all have a question that drives us,\u201d opined Vigil.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The conversation died away. Vigil seemed comfortable to remain in a thoughtful silence and Pomponia took her leave. She returned to her current home, a tiny room in the top floor of an apartment block, the events of the evening (and the prophecy she had paid for) running through her mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The first session was quite info-dumpy and navel-gazey; we're both finding our feet with Promethean, online one-to-one play and playing a game set in a radically different time period. Future games will hopefully be a bit more exciting, but they're still going to be very dialogue heavy as this is very much the preferred style of both me and the player. His approach is always social/diplomatic first and he loves a big cast of NPCs to bounce off. It'll be interesting to see how the same character plays when walking the path of Iron or Copper!</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}